+## Natural Core Motion - source candidate v0.1 (29 October 2026)
+
+**B - Observers & Diagnostics -> Natural Core Motion** adds an explicit passive
+observation of a selected, validated three-channel Core RunRecord. Analyze the
+stored history, then inspect attached face vectors and their collective turn,
+conditional Z with frozen and staged observer settings, and separate native,
+envelope and clock displacement contributions. A common-phase probe transforms
+a display copy. The accepted host wire and declared refined PLUS tau=0 surface
+stay fixed.
+
+This is a separately identified application observation component; it computes
+the displayed correspondences from stored states without stepping the native
+recurrence or changing the kernel, worker, clocks, records or artifact locks.
+The staged display observer is explicitly recomputed and remains separate from
+recorded staged/EMA outputs. Source and edit guards qualify retained caches;
+JSON export preserves the completed observation's parent and configuration.
+
+Read the [feature guide](NATURAL_CORE_MOTION_v0.1.md) for controls, numerical
+limits, exact-value inspection and export behaviour, and the accompanying
+[research draft source](../../papers/NATURAL_CORE_MOTION_CORRESPONDENCE/v0.1/main.tex)
+for the correspondence and its limits. The candidate has 23 passing component/
+mathematical checks and 13 passing offscreen Qt panel checks. Its MainWindow
+smoke used a test-only installed-kernel-lock stub. These Linux source checks do
+not certify the Windows CPython 3.11 locked installation or real Windows export.
+
+**This is an uninstalled source candidate, not a package release or an accepted
+material-core motion law.** Earlier release and certification statements below
+retain their original scope.
+
 
 ## Paper G axial observations (APP-G1 / APP-G2 / APP-G3)
 
